WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.355
Imagine your family's income rises. You might buy more takeaway pizzas and fewer budget biscuits. Income changes demand.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:21.947
Income elasticity of demand, or Y E D, divides the percentage change in quantity demanded by the percentage change in income. Quantity on top, income underneath.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:33.681
The answer tells you the type of good. Below nought is inferior. Nought to one is a normal good that is a necessity. Above one is a luxury.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:41.692
For a luxury, demand grows faster than income. Income up ten per cent, demand up twenty per cent: Y E D is two.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:53.424
Step one. Write both changes with signs. Income rises five per cent, and demand for cheap noodles falls two per cent.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:06.057
Step two. Divide quantity by income. Minus two divided by five is minus nought point four. Step three: round if asked, and add no per cent sign.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:18.711
Step four. Classify. Minus nought point four is below nought, so cheap noodles are an inferior good. As incomes rise, demand shifts left.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:35.223
Here is a real question from June 2024. Income increases by seven per cent and quantity demanded increases by eleven per cent. Calculate Y E D to two decimal places. Two marks.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:41.678
Both changes are rises, so both are plus. Income plus seven, quantity plus eleven.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:50.742
Quantity on top. Eleven divided by seven is one point five seven one four. To two decimal places, one point five seven.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:02:06.323
One point five seven is above one: demand grows faster than income, so this is a luxury good. The question did not ask for this, but it is good practice. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:15.225
A common mistake is putting income on top. Seven over eleven gives the wrong answer.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:22.428
Another is calling a value between nought and one a luxury. That is a normal good, a necessity.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:41.328
Now you try. Incomes fall by four per cent, and demand for a supermarket's value bread rises by three per cent. Calculate Y E D to two decimal places, and name the type of good. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.706
Income fell, so minus four. Demand rose, so plus three.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:56.447
Plus three divided by minus four is minus nought point seven five. It is negative, so the bread is an inferior good.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:06.145
Remember: quantity change over income change, keep the signs, round as asked, then classify. Now try the practice questions.
